.TH CCLOCK 1
.SH NAME
cclock \- draggable countdown overlay for Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cclock
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cclock
displays a countdown in a layer-shell overlay attached to a screen edge.
Drag the overlay to move it between edges and outputs, click it to pause or
resume, and hover over it to reveal the configured text and close button.
.PP
If no duration is supplied, cclock opens a time picker.  Time values supplied
with different options are added together.  At zero, cclock beeps and continues
to display elapsed overtime with a leading plus sign.
.PP
Control and query options communicate with the running cclock instance.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help-all
Display command-line help, including generic Qt options, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-picker
Open the time picker even when a duration was supplied.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-seconds " " \fINUM\fR
Add NUM seconds to the countdown.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-minutes " " \fINUM\fR
Add NUM minutes to the countdown.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-hours " " \fINUM\fR
Add NUM hours to the countdown.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-text " " \fITEXT\fR
Show TEXT while the overlay is hovered.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-stop
Stop the running instance and exit.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-time-get
Print the running instance's time without a leading minute zero and exit.  With
.BR \-\-stop ,
print the time before stopping it.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-text-get
Print the running instance's text and exit.  With
.BR \-\-stop ,
print the text before stopping it.  This option cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-time-get .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-color " " \fICOLOR\fR
Set the running overlay color.  COLOR must be an opaque Qt color name or hex
value.  The default is #0b0b0d.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-pause-color " " \fICOLOR\fR
Set the paused overlay color.  COLOR must be an opaque Qt color name or hex
value.  The default is #ffd60a.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send a desktop notification when this instance is stopped from the overlay or
through a control command.
.TP
.B \-\-pause
Pause the running instance.
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Resume the running instance.
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Toggle the running instance between paused and running.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cclock/cclock.conf
Saved edge position and last picker value.  If
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset, Qt normally uses
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cclock.sock
Local socket used to control the running instance.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested operation succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
No running instance accepted a control or query request, or startup failed.
.TP
.B 2
The supplied duration, color, or option combination was invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cclock -m 25 -t \(dqWrite tests\(dq
Start a 25-minute countdown with hover text.
.TP
.B cclock -m 1 -s 30 -c steelblue -C '#ffd60a'
Start a 90-second countdown with custom running and paused colors.
.TP
.B cclock --stop --time-get
Print the displayed time, then stop the running instance.
